// CAS-both+rel+acq.
//
// Two CASes from the initial value both succeed.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   the models' definitions:
//     SC forbids. Two RMWs read the same write, which RMW atomicity forbids.
//     VbD forbids. Two RMWs read the same write, which RMW atomicity forbids.
//     TSO forbids. Two RMWs read the same write, which RMW atomicity forbids.
//     x86-TSO forbids. Two RMWs read the same write, which RMW atomicity
//       forbids.
//     ClightTSO forbids. Two RMWs read the same write, which RMW atomicity
//       forbids.
//     Coherence allows. Coherence has no atomicity axiom, and the two writes to
//       x can be ordered either way.
//     RC11 forbids. Two RMWs read the same write, which RMW atomicity forbids.
//     RC11z forbids. Two RMWs read the same write, which RMW atomicity forbids.
//     RA forbids. Two RMWs read the same write, which RMW atomicity forbids.
//     SRA forbids. Two RMWs read the same write, which RMW atomicity forbids.
//     WRA forbids. WRA's weak atomicity: no two RMWs read one write.
//     CC allows. CC is stated over plain reads and writes and has no RMW axiom;
//       it is where CC and WRA part.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: RC17, OD-LSO, MRD,
//     PC, PRAM, Causal, Slow, Local, POCausal, RYW, MR, MW, WFR.
x := 0;
{
  rpx := &x;
  r0 := CAS(acq, rel, rpx, 0, 1)
} ||| {
  rpy := &x;
  r1 := CAS(acq, rel, rpy, 0, 2)
}
%%
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 1) [Coherence, CC]
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 1) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, RC11, RC11z, RA,
                           SRA, WRA]
